The column graph shows students' preferred ways of travelling to school.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=12mm,y=1mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,44);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(5,0);
\foreach \v in {0,10,20,30,40} {\draw[black] (-0.08,\v)--(0,\v); \node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-0.08,\v) {$\v$};}
\foreach \x/\h/\name in {1/30/Car,2/35/Bus,3/10/Walk,4/25/Bike} {\draw[black] (\x-0.3,0) rectangle (\x+0.3,\h); \node[below] at (\x,0) {\name};}
\node[rotate=90] at (-0.85,22) {Number of students};
\node at (2.5,-10) {Transport};
\node at (2.5,50) {Travel to school};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

a. Which method was most popular, and which was least popular?
b. How many more students travelled by bus than by car?

The graph shows room temperatures measured at hourly intervals.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=13mm,y=1.5mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{seriesblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,27);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(4.5,0);
\foreach \v in {0,5,10,15,20,25} {\draw[black] (-0.08,\v)--(0,\v); \node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-0.08,\v) {$\v$};}
\foreach \x/\label in {0/9 am,1/10 am,2/11 am,3/12 pm,4/1 pm} {\draw[black] (\x,0)--(\x,-0.6); \node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,-0.6) {\label};}
\draw[seriesblue,thick] (0,11)--(1,14)--(2,21)--(3,23)--(4,19);
\foreach \x/\y in {0/11,1/14,2/21,3/23,4/19} {\fill[seriesblue] (\x,\y) circle (1.8pt);}
\node[rotate=90] at (-0.8,13) {Temperature ($^{\circ}$C)};
\node at (2,-7) {Time};
\node at (2,31) {Room temperature};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

a. Describe the temperature trend.
b. Between which measurements did the temperature increase the most?
c. Does the graph support the conclusion that the temperature increased by the same amount each hour?

The graph shows a device's battery level at three measurements one hour apart.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=15mm,y=0.5mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,106);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(4,0);
\foreach \v in {0,20,40,60,80,100} {\draw[black] (-0.07,\v)--(0,\v); \node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-0.07,\v) {$\v$};}
\foreach \x/\h/\label in {1/80/Start,2/50/Hour 1,3/20/Hour 2} {\draw[black] (\x-0.28,0) rectangle (\x+0.28,\h); \node[below] at (\x,0) {\label};}
\node[rotate=90] at (-0.75,50) {Battery (\%)};
\node at (2,-20) {Time};
\node at (2,118) {Device battery};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Explain whether each conclusion is supported.
a. The starting battery level was four times the level at hour 2.
b. The battery level fell by 30 percentage points from the start to hour 2.
c. The battery level fell by the same amount in each displayed one-hour interval.

Each student ran the same 100 m course. The graph shows their finishing times.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=12mm,y=1.6mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,27);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(5,0);
\foreach \v in {0,5,10,15,20,25} {\draw[black] (-0.08,\v)--(0,\v); \node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-0.08,\v) {$\v$};}
\foreach \x/\h/\label in {1/18/A,2/24/B,3/16/C,4/21/D} {\draw[black] (\x-0.3,0) rectangle (\x+0.3,\h); \node[below] at (\x,0) {\label};}
\node[rotate=90] at (-0.8,13) {Time (seconds)};
\node at (2.5,-6) {Student};
\node at (2.5,31) {Times to run 100 m};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Sam says, "B was fastest because B has the tallest column." Explain why Sam is incorrect and identify the fastest student.
